WEBVTT

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.650
Manager Zaizen, is that…

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:12.030
Yes, there’s no doubt.  It’s an Ignis.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:13.630
They're coming!

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.070
A duelist with an Ignis…

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.600
Who is he?

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.710
Bring it on!  I’ll face 
you both simultaneously!

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:32.000
Prepare yourself.  Soulburner 
never shows mercy.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.070
He'll shut you down!

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.780
I didn’t go that far.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.560
Really?

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.690
Stop saying whatever you want!

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.660
Are you really an AI?

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:46.430
Of course.  I’m an AI 
born to be your partner.

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:48.930
It's ten years since I was given life.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:53.640
My name in kanji means "indomitable 
soul dream."  Pronounced "Flame."

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:54.780
Cool, right?

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.780
I've heard that explanation 10,000 times.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:00.250
I’ve only said it 37 times.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.400
The fire Ignis has shown itself.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.390
Saved us the effort of finding it.

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:09.390
Yeah.  Change of plans.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.600
Retrieve that fire ignis.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.610
Let’s use our special strategy.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.610
Combining sequence...

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:17.720
...begin!

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:18.800
What?

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.810
Combination complete.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.380
We are Bit.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:35.040
We are Boot.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.260
Combined…

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:37.520
BitBoot!

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.990
Unbelievable!  They combined!

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:43.990
How good for you, Soulburner.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:46.990
Seems like it'll be a fun duel.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:09.300
Our lives aren't forever

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:16.110
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:23.420
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:29.990
Sharing hope for the future

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:36.730
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:43.970
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:50.680
I want to share your pain

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:23.420
What?  They combined!

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:27.250
Never mind that!  The fire 
duelist smells like a scoop!

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.100
After them!

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.650
Understood!

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.490
Speed Duel!

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:38.040
We’ll go first.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.430
We summon D-Scale Saber 
Sardine from our hand.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:48.030
Saber Sardine’s effect activates.

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:53.420
We pay 500 LP to Special 
Summon a D-Scale Token.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.150
Appear!

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:57.120
Our circuit!

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:00.860
The summoning conditions are two D-Scales.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:06.030
We set D-Scale Token and Saber 
Sardine in the Link Markers!

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:08.290
Link Summon!

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:13.650
Appear, Link 2 D-Scale Battle Coela!

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.070
What'll they do now?

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:21.040
From our hand, we activate the 
Equip Spell, D-Scale Torpedo.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:24.050
We equip it on Battle Coela.

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:28.240
D-Scale Battle Coela’s effect activates.

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:34.920
Once per turn, Battle Coela moves to 
the Main Monster Zone it points to.

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:38.080
They moved their Link Monster.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.120
Yeah.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:42.400
Activate Skill, Marker’s Portal!

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:47.310
Once during the duel, when our LP are 
equal or lower than our original points...

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:51.420
...we select one Link Spell 
in our deck and activate it!

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.220
Three arrows, shine!

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.660
Fire at the enemy who blocks our way!

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.360
The Link Spell, Judgment Arrows!

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:05.090
When the Link Monster linked to this 
card battles, its ATK are doubled.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:11.960
But if Judgment Arrows leaves the field, all 
monsters next to its links are destroyed.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:16.050
A Skill that activates a 
Link Spell from their deck!

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:19.130
They also use Judgment Arrows?

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.980
Playmaker's opponent used that card.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:26.290
Yeah.  As did the enemy who 
destroyed my homeworld.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:28.690
And also Cyberse-Type.

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:31.210
I'll never forgive them!

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:35.090
So if we defeat them, we 
may be able to get info.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:38.050
Next, Battle Coela’s effect activates.

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:44.160
Once per turn, Battle Coela can move next 
to the link of a card it’s linked to.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:48.650
Battle Coela moves next to 
Judgment Arrows’s link.

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:51.360
They moved it again.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:54.370
Quake in fear, Soulburner.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:56.630
We’ll show you a wonderous combo.

00:05:56.630 --> 00:06:01.570
D-Scale Torpedo, equipped to Battle 
Coela, activates its effect!

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:07.170
Every time the equipped monster moved 
this turn, you take 800 damage.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:12.130
There's a card that changes 
movement into damage?

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:13.060
Here it comes!

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:16.060
Battle Coela moved twice.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.540
So you take 1600 damage!

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:31.170
Battle Coela, Torpedo and Judgment 
Arrows form the mightiest combo.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:34.140
We named it "Voyage to Hell."

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:37.950
Whenever Battle Coela moves, quake in fear.

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.410
We end our turn.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:44.690
You can't battle on the first turn, but 
they already dealt a lot of damage.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:46.900
It really is a voyage to hell.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.980
This is bad, Soulburner.

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:52.640
If they move their monster 
three more times, we lose.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:55.640
I’ll break that combo first!

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:58.380
My turn!  I draw!

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:02.250
I set one card.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:07.090
I activate Salamangreat 
Mia’s effect from my hand!

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:13.550
By discarding a Salamangreat 
monster, it Special Summons itself!

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:18.020
The Salamangreat Foxy I discarded 
activates its effect!

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:21.890
When there’s a faceup spell 
or trap card on the field...

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:27.770
...by discarding one Salamangreat, 
it Special Summons itself!

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:35.440
Then a faceup spell or 
trap card is destroyed!

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:38.420
I destroy Judgment Arrows!

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:42.320
That's quite an interesting card.

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:43.840
But worthless.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:48.420
When I use my Skill Marker's 
Portal to bring out a card...

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:51.320
...it can’t be destroyed 
by your card effects!

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:53.680
Seriously?

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:54.770
Don’t give up!

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:58.010
Sink your teeth and open a path!

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:00.650
Be quiet!  I was just a bit surprised!

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:02.770
Besides, I still have options.

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:06.300
I activate Salamangreat Falco’s 
effect from my graveyard!

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:09.730
By returning a Salamangreat 
on the field to my hand...

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:12.040
...it Special Summons itself!

00:08:14.070 --> 00:08:17.520
Then Mia that was added to 
my hand activates its effect.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:23.440
When it's added to my hand other than by 
a usual draw, it Special Summons itself!

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:26.970
I’m getting fired up!

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:31.000
Now that I have three monsters, 
I'll give it my all!

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.570
I'll Link Summon!

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:33.680
So do it.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:35.300
This is where I come in?

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:39.560
Appear!  The circuit that changes the future!

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:46.680
The summoning conditions are at 
least two Fire Effect Monsters.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:53.410
I set Salamangreat Falco, Foxy 
and Mia in the Link Markers!

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:55.020
Link Summon!

00:08:55.770 --> 00:09:00.810
Appear, Link 3 Salamangreat Heatlio!

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:08.070
There it is.

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:10.430
So that’s your ace monster.

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:12.920
Heatlio’s effect activates!

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:15.570
When Heatlio is Link Summoned...

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:19.700
...a card in your Spell and 
Trap Zone returns to your deck!

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:24.080
I can't destroy Judgment Arrows, 
but this'll get rid of it!

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:24.910
What?

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:27.020
Resounding Roar!

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:34.720
When Judgment Arrows leaves the field…

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:39.120
All monsters next to its links are destroyed!

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:41.320
Battle Coela is gone!

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:46.010
Their field is empty.

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:47.860
Go, Soulburner!

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:52.920
Battle!  Salamangreat Heatlio 
attacks you directly!

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:01.190
Yeah!  I end my turn!

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:03.810
He’s cool!

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:08.810
That fire duelist has what it takes 
to be LINK VRAINS’s newest hero!

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:12.590
I smell a scoop and a bonus!

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:15.360
Let’s sink our teeth into this!

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:26.070
Manager Zaizen, the cards in this 
duel aren't in our database.

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:29.040
They're Cyberse cards.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:34.480
Was he involved in the 
incident ten years ago?

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:37.480
Not bad, Soulburner.

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:39.890
But our specialty begins now.

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:43.590
We will pummel you into hell.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:45.800
It’s our turn!  We draw!

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:52.850
We summon D-Scale Piercing 
Saury from our hand!

00:10:55.460 --> 00:11:00.940
By discarding a Saber Sardine, D-Scale 
Piercing Saury’s effect activates.

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:07.190
We Special Summon a D-Scale monster 
from the graveyard by halving its ATK.

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:11.120
Resurrect, D-Scale Battle Coela!

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:18.460
Quake in fear, Soulburner.

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:22.080
Obeserve the true power of our combination.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:24.900
Activate Skill, Marker’s Portal!

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:26.030
What?

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:28.010
Three arrows, shine!

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:31.740
Again I activate the Link 
Spell, Judgment Arrows!

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:34.450
How can they use a Skill twice?

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:37.710
A Skill can only be used 
once during a Speed Duel!

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.360
You’re correct.

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:43.120
Bit used the Skill last time.

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:45.820
This time, Boot used the Skill.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:48.060
That's cheating!

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:49.790
Appear!

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:51.760
Our circuit!

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:55.760
The summoning conditions 
are at least two D-Scales.

00:11:56.140 --> 00:12:01.860
We set D-Scale Piercing Saury and Link 
2 Battle Coela in the Link Markers!

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:04.310
Link Summon!

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:09.810
Appear, Link 3 D-Scale Full Metal Dunkle!

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:18.470
It’s unbelievably huge!

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:20.960
They’re going crazy!

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:28.160
We set one card.

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:31.400
Full Metal Dunkle, prepare for bombardment.

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:34.400
Charging energy.

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:42.610
Battle!  Full Metal Dunkle attacks Heatlio!

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:48.580
Due to the Link Spell Judgment 
Arrows, its ATK are doubled.

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:54.850
Sink, Soulburner!

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:11.950
We...

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:13.140
...Win.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.230
Too bad.

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:20.550
What?

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:22.660
How are you alive?

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:25.890
I activate the trap, Energy of Fire!

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:32.860
I return a Salamangreat in my graveyard 
to my deck to regain LP equal to its ATK.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:36.770
And my monster isn’t destroyed in battle!

00:13:42.830 --> 00:13:45.540
I activated this card.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.780
So annoying!

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:52.290
But Soulburner is barely alive.

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:54.780
Thanks to your Skill, Boot.

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:57.790
Because you drew good cards, Bit.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:01.250
We'll definitely possess the Ignis.

00:14:01.510 --> 00:14:02.990
We end our turn.

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:05.550
You did well to survive, Soulburner.

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:09.090
But your fate depends on this next draw!

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:12.070
I know that!  My turn!

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:16.910
If I don’t do something about 
Full Metal Dunkle this turn...

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:22.140
...Judgment Arrows will 
double its ATK next turn.

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:25.010
I bet it all on this draw!

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:30.480
Nice!

00:14:31.190 --> 00:14:32.380
From my hand-

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:34.910
Too bad.  You can’t use that card.

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:35.730
What?

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:39.630
We activate the trap, D-Scale Chaff.

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:42.940
It activates when a D-Scale Link 
Monster has Link Markers...

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:49.340
...equal to the number of cards in your hand 
plus the number of monsters on your field.

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:51.940
Full Metal Dunkle is Link 3.

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:55.060
You have two cards in your hand, 
and one monster on your field.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:56.310
That totals three.

00:14:57.570 --> 00:15:02.750
When this card activates, your 
hand and your monster's effects...

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:05.360
...are negated until the end of this turn.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:08.220
And Heatlio isn’t allowed to attack.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:09.970
Lock complete.

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:14.330
You can’t use your ace monster 
or the two cards in your hand.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:17.440
We are the mightiest.

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:19.540
We are invincible.

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:23.270
If your hand and monsters are locked…

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:26.100
Surrender, Soulburner.

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:28.150
Hand over the Ignis.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:31.430
You think you already won?

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:35.260
I can’t be wasting my time here!

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:37.520
You're eager to fight!

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:40.730
Soulburner, show them your duel!

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.900
In this situation…

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:44.590
...what can you do?

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:47.570
I'll burn up everyone in my way!

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:53.940
I activate my Skill!

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:55.930
I lower my LP to 100!

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:59.780
For every 1000 LP that I 
gave up, I draw one card!

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:04.150
Get fired up, Soulburner!

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:06.820
Open the closed future!

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.120
Burning Draw!

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.790
It’s a hot card!

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:20.790
I activate the Field Spell, 
Salamangreat Sanctuary!

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:30.880
Good.  Since it’s a new card you drew, 
the trap D-Scale Chaff can't lock it down!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.880
You're resisting in vain.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:37.120
What can you do with a single card?

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:38.750
I’ll show you!

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:42.480
This is Link Summoning's new potential!

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:50.460
Surging flame, awaken Heatlio’s true 
strength with the power of purification!

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:53.570
Reincarnation Link Summon!

00:16:57.070 --> 00:17:01.870
Resurrect, the king of beasts that 
runs through the fire prairie!

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:04.710
Salamangreat Heatlio!

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:10.700
What?

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:12.720
Awesome!

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:15.720
Boss, what happened?

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:16.950
Umm…

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:22.390
Heatlio’s summoning conditions should 
be at least two Fire Effect Monsters.

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:25.120
Reincarnation Link Summon?

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:27.100
What's that?

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:33.100
Due to Salamangreat Sanctuary’s effect, 
when I Link Summon a Salamangreat Link Monster...

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:38.810
...I can use a monster with the same name 
instead of Link Materials to Link Summon!

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:43.180
He used Heatlio to summon a new Heatlio!

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:48.320
And D-Scale Chaff can't affect 
the reincarnated Heatlio!

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:50.530
Heatlio’s effect activates!

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:53.290
Judgment Arrows returns to your deck!

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:55.510
Resounding Roar!

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:59.060
We got this!

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:01.800
Since Judgment Arrows leaves the field...

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:04.380
...Full Metal Dunkle that's 
next to its link is destroyed!

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:05.440
Wrong!

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:07.840
Full Metal Dunkle’s effect activates.

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:10.840
Once per turn, its destruction is negated...

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:14.940
...and it moves to a Main 
Monster Zone next to its link.

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:17.620
When Full Metal Dunkle moves...

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:22.180
...it destroys a monster vertical 
to it at the end of this turn!

00:18:22.180 --> 00:18:25.190
We destroy Heatlio.

00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:30.240
If Heatlio is gone, you have 
no monsters to defend with.

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:34.130
Full Metal Dunkle will end you next turn.

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:36.500
It’s over.

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:40.340
Heatlio can’t destroy Full Metal Dunkle.

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:42.880
They'll take me-

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:45.170
No, Flame.  You're wrong.

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:47.080
This match is already over!

00:18:47.840 --> 00:18:50.080
Heatlio’s effect activates!

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:54.020
When it’s Reincarnation Link 
Summoned, for one time only...

00:18:54.020 --> 00:19:00.160
...one of your monster's ATK becomes 
the same as a monster in my graveyard!

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:02.200
Flame Possession!

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:07.600
Full Metal Dunkle’s ATK become 
the same as my graveyard's Mia!

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:12.140
800 ATK?

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:13.300
No way!

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:17.910
Battle!  Heatlio attacks Full Metal Dunkle!

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:21.710
Heat Soul!

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:45.570
I knew you were no match for us.

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:49.110
Didn't you just say it was all over for you?

00:19:50.780 --> 00:19:52.830
What’s wrong, Soulburner?

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:56.540
Burning Draw is hard on me.

00:19:56.860 --> 00:20:00.790
Of course it is.  That Skill 
lowers your LP to 100.

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:03.640
Can't you be a bit more sympathetic?

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:08.580
Did it hurt, Soulburner?  Oh, how sad.

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:10.030
I change my mind.

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:14.180
It’s your fault we lost, Bit.

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:16.030
That’s what I should be saying!

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:17.720
You’re useless.

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:19.510
No, I’m using you.

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:21.120
Bit, you’re fired!

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:22.880
No, you’re fired, Boot!

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:24.240
You’re both fired!

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:26.320
You are fired!

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:27.250
Fire?

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:30.780
Useless.

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:31.790
Wait!

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:34.280
He's persistent.

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:39.760
Brother, we're almost there.  Hang on.

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:49.630
Give up, Playmaker.

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:52.180
Jin Kusanagi’s data is ours.

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:54.670
Stop joking! Why are you doing this?

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:57.670
Something unbelievable will happen soon.

00:20:57.670 --> 00:20:59.420
Stay tuned.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:04.040
Warning: This area is restricted.

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:06.360
You can't go any further.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:09.750
Warning: This area is restricted.

00:21:09.970 --> 00:21:11.730
You can no longer escape!

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:16.780
What?

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:24.340
Playmaker!

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:29.220
How did they get through the restricted area?

00:21:31.360 --> 00:21:35.820
Restricted area has been accessed illegally.

00:21:35.820 --> 00:21:39.250
Activating emergency defense program.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:40.600
This is bad.

00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:42.450
I’m logging out.

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:44.590
You should leave too.

00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:45.530
Wait!

00:21:45.850 --> 00:21:47.260
What’s your name?

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:50.260
I’m Soulburner.

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:51.760
Until we meet again.

00:21:53.980 --> 00:21:55.760
Soulburner...

00:21:55.760 --> 00:21:57.760
Who is he?

00:22:19.930 --> 00:22:26.240
Memories that don't disappear
And memories that disappeared

00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:32.950
I quietly "NOW LOADING..." those scenes

00:22:33.410 --> 00:22:36.450
Memories left behind  Erased memories

00:22:36.450 --> 00:22:39.590
What was the PASSWORD again?

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.190
ACCESS records  Restored memories

00:22:44.480 --> 00:22:47.160
Challenge "the you inside you"

00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:58.040
You're a Network  The 
World that spreads beyond

00:22:58.200 --> 00:23:01.180
With repeating "nows"

00:23:01.530 --> 00:23:05.110
What about you?  "Live for now"

00:23:05.310 --> 00:23:11.090
Grab the Shooting Star in 
the sky with both your hands

00:23:11.240 --> 00:23:14.360
Overcome "now" with all your might  Yell!

00:23:36.300 --> 00:23:40.350
The alarm rings, flustering him.

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:46.100
The restricted area blocked his 
way, and the culprits escaped.

00:23:46.100 --> 00:23:50.170
Without a lead, Yusaku 
returns to the real world.

00:23:50.170 --> 00:23:56.180
That's when a man arrives, 
revealing that he's Soulburner.

00:23:56.180 --> 00:23:58.690
How do you know my identity?

00:23:58.690 --> 00:24:02.570
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Transfer Student Takeru Homura

00:24:02.570 --> 00:24:04.860
Into the VRAINS!
